# Normalize line endings: Git stores text with LF and checks it out with LF on
# every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored trees (machine-readable specifications, mapping schemas, test
# corpora) are exempt from GitHub language statistics and collapse in diffs.
# Nothing is vendored yet; extend the list in the same change that lands the
# first vendored tree (.claude/rules/vendored-inputs.md).
#
# Vendored material is stored byte for byte as its publisher ships it, so it
# also opts out of line-ending normalization and the tree matches the upstream
# archive exactly.
# <path>/vendor/** linguist-vendored
# <path>/vendor/** -text

# The mermaid browser assets the book loads, fetched verbatim by
# scripts/vendor/mdbook-mermaid-assets.sh (website/book/vendor/mermaid/PROVENANCE.md).
website/book/vendor/mermaid/*.js linguist-vendored
website/book/vendor/mermaid/*.js -text
website/book/vendor/mermaid/LICENSE-* linguist-vendored

# The brand rasters are binary. `text=auto` above detects that by itself, and
# the explicit opt-out keeps a future misdetection from rewriting their bytes
# (assets/brand/README.md).
*.png -text
*.ico -text

# A generated tree is marked generated so it collapses in diffs and stays out
# of language statistics (.claude/rules/codegen.md). The one generated tree the
# architecture calls for is the OMOP CDM v5.4 row types and DDL emitted from
# the OHDSI CommonDataModel definitions (docs/architecture.md section 7). The
# `omop-cdm` crate is mixed, so only the emitted subtree is marked, never the
# hand-written vocabulary loader and resolver beside it. The path is reserved
# here so it is in force before the first generated file lands.
crates/omop-cdm/src/generated/** linguist-generated
